You are in a winter garden. There is a fountain, a small glasshouse in the east direction and a door on the west. The man is sitting on a bench.

> speak to man

The old man is happy that you are back. "Let's play!"

You chose to play white and decided to use one of the tactics described in a book. It seems like the man noticed, but did not show that. So you don't know if he just let you win or it was your achievement. Nevermind.

The old man looks pretty happy.
"Thank you for playing with me. It was a pleasure. I will open you the front door, so you can leave whenever you want."

The man slowly stands up and goes in the direction of the entrance. But then he suddenly stops, turns to you and says:

"You know, you can stay here as long as you want. The house is much bigger than this garden, and you can meet many magical creatures. What do you think?"

1: "Hm, sounds like a good idea!"
2: "No, thank you, I would like to return to my house."
> 2
You politely refuse the proposal. The old man sighs and walks away.
